    {
      "id": "vrt_casebook",
      "cell": [
        5,
        16
      ],
      "kind": "book",
      "label": "A casebook on the table",
      "model": "book",
      "codex": "van_richten_casebook",
      "flag": "van_richten_notes_read",
      "text": "Casebook, Barovia, in a small, precise hand. 'S. is old, patient, and bored, and boredom is the only weakness I have seen him show. He cannot cross running water of his own will. He must be asked in, once. Sunlight undoes him. A stake holds him, it does not end him: that wants the sun, or the blade the cards keep hiding. He reads what people write about him. I am writing this anyway.' Lower down: 'The wolves in the hills above Zarovich answer to him through their leader, a brute called Kiril. Their old leader would not. I have marked the den on the map.' And in the margin, underlined twice: 'The lantern-room ward drinks from the copper rod in the hearth. PULL IT before you go up, you old fool. You nearly cooked yourself in the spring.'"
    },
    {
      "id": "vrt_disguise_ledger",
      "cell": [
        9,
        16
      ],
      "kind": "book",
      "label": "A ledger of disguises",
      "model": "ledger",
      "codex": "van_richten_disguises",
      "flag": "van_richten_identity_known",
      "text": "A ledger of costumes, each with a name, a town and a date. The last entry is fresh: 'RICTAVIO. Vallaki, the Blue Water Inn. A half-elf showman, loud, harmless, forgettable. Scarlet coat; the hat does the rest. The tiger travels as the act. Nobody looks twice at a man who wants to be looked at.'"
    },
    {
      "id": "vrt_valley_map",
